  <!-- ===== Onboarding Page 1: Welcome ===== -->
  <data name="OnboardingTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Welcome to VoiceGarden</value></data>
  <data name="NeuralTTSForSAPI" xml:space="preserve"><value>Neural TTS for Windows SAPI</value></data>
  <data name="WhatIsVoiceGarden" xml:space="preserve"><value>What is VoiceGarden?</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingDesc1" xml:space="preserve"><value>VoiceGarden is a free, open-source voice bridge that connects 20+ modern text-to-speech engines to any Windows application that supports SAPI 5 — including Grid 3, Mind Express, Balabolka, Tobii Communicator, and any app built on System.Speech.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingDesc2" xml:space="preserve"><value>It works by registering as a standard SAPI 5 voice. Once installed, your AAC and accessibility software can use high-quality neural voices — both offline and cloud-based — without any code changes.</value></data>
  <data name="Feature20Engines" xml:space="preserve"><value>✔  20+ engines: SherpaOnnx, Azure, Edge, OpenAI, Google, ElevenLabs, Polly</value></data>
  <data name="FeatureOffline" xml:space="preserve"><value>✔  Fully offline with SherpaOnnx neural models</value></data>
  <data name="FeatureWordBoundary" xml:space="preserve"><value>✔  Word boundary events for highlighting</value></data>
  <data name="FeatureDualArch" xml:space="preserve"><value>✔  Works with both 32-bit and 64-bit applications</value></data>

  <!-- ===== Onboarding Page 2: How To Use ===== -->
  <data name="GettingStarted" xml:space="preserve"><value>Getting Started</value></data>
  <data name="Step1Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Install the SAPI Adapter</value></data>
  <data name="Step1Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>On the main screen, click Install for 64-bit (and 32-bit if needed). This registers VoiceGarden as a SAPI 5 voice that any compatible app can use.</value></data>
  <data name="Step2Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Download SherpaOnnx Voices (Offline)</value></data>
  <data name="Step2Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Go to the SherpaOnnx Models tab to browse and download free neural voices. These run entirely on your device — no internet connection needed. After downloading, click Promote to make them available to SAPI applications.</value></data>
  <data name="LangCompatTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>💡  Tip: Language Compatibility</value></data>
  <data name="LangCompatDesc" xml:space="preserve"><value>If your AAC software only supports certain languages (e.g. English), enable "Add en-US alias" when promoting SherpaOnnx models. This makes voices in any language appear as English voices, so they show up in apps that filter by language.</value></data>
  <data name="Step3Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Add Cloud Engine Keys (Optional)</value></data>
  <data name="Step3Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>For premium cloud voices (Azure, OpenAI, Google, ElevenLabs, Polly), go to the Cloud Engines tab and enter your API key. Edge voices work without any key.</value></data>

  <!-- ===== Onboarding Page 3: Privacy ===== -->
  <data name="HelpImprove" xml:space="preserve"><value>Help Improve VoiceGarden</value></data>
  <data name="PrivacyIntro" xml:space="preserve"><value>VoiceGarden is a free, open-source project built by volunteers. To help us understand which TTS engines are most used, identify bugs, and prioritise development, we'd like to collect anonymous usage analytics.</value></data>
  <data name="WhatWeCollect" xml:space="preserve"><value>What we collect:</value></data>
  <data name="WhatWeCollectList" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Engine types enabled
• Number of models downloaded
• Adapter registration events</value></data>
  <data name="WhatWeDontCollect" xml:space="preserve"><value>What we DON'T collect:</value></data>
  <data name="WhatWeDontCollectList" xml:space="preserve"><value>• Spoken text or audio content
• API keys or credentials
• Voice names or personal information</value></data>
  <data name="PrivacyChangeAnytime" xml:space="preserve"><value>You can change this anytime in Settings → Advanced.</value></data>
  <data name="YesHelpImprove" xml:space="preserve"><value>Yes, help improve VoiceGarden</value></data>
  <data name="NoThanks" xml:space="preserve"><value>No thanks</value></data>

